jQuery already provides a number of [global ajax events](http://docs.jquery.com/Ajax_Events) that correspond with local ajax events. But there is no global complement for `beforeSend`. `ajaxSend` is similar, but is triggered after the request is opened so it can not be canceled cleanly.
## Use Cases

Bind multiple global handlers to `beforeSend` that aren't overridden by local `$.ajax` options.

```
$(document).bind('ajaxBeforeSend', function(e, xhr, settings){
  if (settings.dataType === undefined){
    xhr.setRequestHeader('accept', '*/*;q=0.5, ' + settings.accepts.script);
  }
});

$.ajax({
  beforeSend: function(){
    // Doesn't clobber global hook
  }
});
```

Add generic validation hook to all forms:

```
$(document).delegate('form', 'ajaxBeforeSend', function(e){
  if (!validateForm(e.target)){
    return false;
  }
});
```
### References

Functions similar to the custom `ajax:beforeSend` event provided by [rails/jquery-ujs](https://github.com/rails/jquery-ujs).

